sentences.l:
The Viscount of Wei left him;
the Viscount of Ji became his slave;
Bi Gan remonstrated and died.

The men of Qi sent a gift of women musicians;
Ji Huanzi accepted them, and for three days there was no court.
Kongzi left.

Of Yu Zhong and Yi Yi he said:
“Living hidden they dwelt, and let their words go;
their persons hit purity, their setting aside hit the right weighing.”

Gan, of the second meal, went to Chu;
Liao, of the third meal, went to Cai;
Que, of the fourth meal, went to Qin.

The Duke of Zhou said to the Duke of Lu:
“The gentleman does not neglect his kin;
he does not let the great ministers resent not being used;
old associates, without grave cause, he does not cast off;
do not demand everything of one man.”
